Expected elements: MISSING — transaction age; transaction type in the overview grid; the 'supply an ABI' action.

Three Must-show items are absent, so those are findings #1–#3, all P1, and the rating is capped at 4. Nothing anywhere on the page states when this transaction happened: the hero carries the eyebrow, truncated hash, `Succeeded` badge and full hash, and the Overview grid runs DATA / BLOCK / CANONICAL / FINALITY / FEE PAYER / TARGET / COST·MANA. No age, no timestamp. Transaction type is not a labelled grid row, though the raw block prints `"kind": "public-avm-call"`. And the Decoded input note says "Supplying an ABI decodes them" while offering no control that does it.

Everything else required is present and I checked provenance independently: the marker is the `Data` row at the top of the facts grid, badge `Synthetic demo data` plus the producer's sentences, exactly one form, no band and none expected. Nav, footer, disclosure and the three drawn marks are all there.

On density: the facts grid delivers six values, so a 1920 viewport holds a page that is mostly canvas and prose. Events / Internal calls / State changes spend roughly 500 px of scroll on three sentences, one of which the trace card already printed. The `Data` row's four-line paragraph is 3.5x the height of every other row, so the grid opens on prose.

Fixes: put age in the hero beside the finality state, and give transaction type its own grid row.

Rating: 4/10

